<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Salisbury sits about twenty minutes west of Moncton along the Petitcodiac River, and a lot of homes and farmhouses out this way still heat with oil. Most of those tanks sit outside year-round, taking everything a New Brunswick winter can throw at them. Freeze-thaw, blowing snow, and spring rain are hard on steel, and an outdoor tank often ages faster than the same tank would in a basement.</p><p>Hub City Tank Co handles <a href="/oil-tank-replacement-moncton/">oil tank replacement</a> and <a href="/oil-tank-removal-moncton/">removal</a> for Salisbury and the rural roads around it. We're licensed and insured, our estimates are free and in writing, and since we're based in Moncton we can usually get out to you quickly. If your tank is leaking right now, skip the reading and call (506) 802-3471. That line is answered 24/7.</p></div></div></section>
